[audit] Reviewed the committed Plan 07 implementation and its prior execution log. The implementation log explicitly leaves HTTP response/WebSocket lifecycle, typed local error delivery, ingress worker ownership, live process cases, bounded fuzz runs, and owner-environment validation incomplete.
[audit] The committed tests/ingress/local.sh always exits 2 after workspace unit tests, so no Plan 07 local real-process case has been certified. Plan 07 cannot yet hand off to the next phase.
[audit] Preserved four pre-existing uncommitted changes in Cargo.lock, crates/p2x-proxy/Cargo.toml, http.rs, and http_io.rs. They begin response-boundary and WebSocket work and are being reviewed as part of the correction.
[validation] cargo fmt --all -- --check and cargo test -p p2x-proxy passed with the preserved candidate changes; 26 p2x-proxy tests passed.
[validation] cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings passed with the preserved candidate changes.
[fix] Completed the HTTP response-side gate, bounded request metadata association, informational/final response handling, close-delimited and fixed/chunked framing, verified WebSocket transition, and typed guard diagnostics.
[fix] Added absolute later-boundary and upgrade decision timers, same-read cross-authority withholding, early-final upload abandonment, and exact response-write acknowledgement after a declined upgrade violation.
[fix] Added bounded pre-forward HTTP status/code/trace responses for parser and setup failures and carried post-forward guard codes into the tunnel terminal.
[fix] Reworked TLS record traversal to process each complete record once and retain record spans over the original wire buffer instead of a second whole-ClientHello allocation; tightened nested SNI length and A-label/IP validation.
[fix] Corrected the checked per-ingress application-buffer formula and sized the ingress transition channel from the shared admission limit; listener-owned connection tasks are now reaped during normal operation.
